From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: Ctrl-C ends --dynamic-interval

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: --dynamic-interval runs until a signal handler exits the
program. On AROS, Ctrl-C is the task's SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C, not a POSIX
SIGINT, so the handler never ran and only closing the window ended it.
Solution: ffTimeSleep waits in Delay() ticks on AROS and returns false
when Ctrl-C arrived; the dynamic loop then leaves and finishes normally,
which restores the console (line wrap, alternate screen) as the handler
would.
Scope: common/time.h (AROS branch) and the dynamic loop in fastfetch.c,
which now also leaves when the sleep reports an interruption on other
systems (there the handler has exited before).
Upstream-Status: the loop change is generic; the sleep is AROS-specific.
Verification: Ctrl-C in Limpet on pool v1-1, v11-1 and rpi-1 (2026-10-27):
the primary screen came back and the Shell got rc 0.
Removal: when the AROS C library delivers Ctrl-C as SIGINT.
---
 src/common/time.h | 8 +++++++-
 src/fastfetch.c   | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/common/time.h b/src/common/time.h
index a4d2534..f88607a 100644
--- a/src/common/time.h
+++ b/src/common/time.h
@@ -51,9 +51,15 @@ static inline uint64_t ffTimeGetNow(void) {
 #endif
 }
 
+#ifdef __AROS__
+    #include "common/aros/aros_sleep.h"
+#endif
+
 // Returns true if not interrupted
 static inline bool ffTimeSleep(uint32_t msec) {
-#ifdef _WIN32
+#ifdef __AROS__
+    return ffArosSleep(msec);
+#elif defined(_WIN32)
     LARGE_INTEGER interval;
     interval.QuadPart = -(int64_t) msec * 10000; // Relative time in 100-nanosecond intervals
     return NT_SUCCESS(NtDelayExecution(TRUE, &interval));
diff --git a/src/fastfetch.c b/src/fastfetch.c
index 583a1f0..ac66156 100644
--- a/src/fastfetch.c
+++ b/src/fastfetch.c
@@ -818,7 +818,12 @@ static void run(FFdata* data) {
             ffLogoPrintRemaining(); // `logoLineCacheClear` inside so that ffLogoPrintLine will use `\e[nC` to move the cursor to the right position instead of reprinting the logo
             fputs("\e[J", stdout); // Clear from cursor to the end of the screen to prevent artifacts when the new output is shorter than the previous one
             fflush(stdout);
-            ffTimeSleep(instance.state.dynamicInterval);
+            if (!ffTimeSleep(instance.state.dynamicInterval)) {
+                // Interrupted where no signal handler ends the program
+                // (Ctrl-C on AROS): finish normally, which restores the
+                // console (ffFinish).
+                break;
+            }
             fputs("\e[H", stdout); // Move cursor to the top left corner to overwrite the previous output
             instance.state.keysHeight = 0; // Reset keysHeight so `ffLogoPrintRemaining` will recalculate it
             ffCacheInvalidateAll(); // Drop the detection results cached for the previous round, so that this round re-detects them
